# Files managed by the KDE profile.  Paths are relative to $HOME.
#
# `setup kde apply` copies repo -> $HOME, `setup kde save` copies $HOME -> repo.
# Copy, not symlink: KConfig rewrites these files on every settings change and
# on logout, using a write-temp-then-rename pattern that a symlink survives only
# by luck. Entries missing on either side are skipped with a notice, so it is
# safe to list a file before it exists.
#
# A trailing "/" means "the whole directory, recursively".
#
# Anything containing an absolute $HOME path is stored with a @HOME@ placeholder
# and substituted on apply/save, so the repo stays portable across machines.

# ── Shortcuts (the .desktop files carry X-KDE-Shortcuts defaults; overrides made
#    in System Settings land in kglobalshortcutsrc and win over them) ──────────
.config/kglobalshortcutsrc
.local/share/applications/dots-arch-logo.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-browser.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-browser-incognito.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-code-editor.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-ocr.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-focus-down.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-focus-left.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-focus-right.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-focus-up.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-office.desktop
# Creado desde Ajustes > Atajos como "atajo de comando": es lo que engancha la
# tecla Meta a KRunner. X-KDE-GlobalAccel-CommandShortcut=true lo marca como tal.
.local/share/applications/net.local.krunner.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-screenshot-save.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-settings.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-snip-to-search.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-task-manager.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-terminal.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-text-editor.desktop
.local/share/applications/dots-volume-mixer.desktop

# ── Brave: recuperar sesión tras el cierre brusco de la sesión de Plasma ────
.config/brave-flags.conf

# ── Utility scripts backing those shortcuts ─────────────────────────────────
.config/kde/scripts/

# ── Login check: warns when a compiled KWin effect stops loading ─────────────
.config/autostart/kde-check-kwin-effects.desktop

# ── Theme assets vendored from third parties (see dots/kde/VENDORED.md) ─────
# Scratchy global theme (KDE Store p/1898344, GPL 3+). Vendored whole: 130 files,
# 2.5 MB, no symlinks. A global theme in Plasma 6 is four separate packages —
# look-and-feel, aurorae decoration, Plasma style and colour scheme — and all
# four must be present or the theme applies half-broken.
.local/share/plasma/look-and-feel/Scratchy/
.local/share/aurorae/themes/Scratchy/
.local/share/plasma/desktoptheme/Scratchy/
.local/share/color-schemes/Scratchy.colors

# scpmk power menu — vendored because it is PATCHED for Plasma 6.7, see VENDORED.md
.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/org.kde.plasma.scpmk/

# Thermal Monitor (store.kde.org/p/998915, upstream invent.kde.org/olib/thermalmonitor,
# MIT, by Oliver Beard). Vendored at 0.2.8 — the AUR package sits at 0.2.7-2 and was
# flagged out-of-date on 2026-07-20, so the Store copy is newer than the packaged one.
.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/org.kde.olib.thermalmonitor/

# Krohnkite tiling KWin script (0.9.9.2, MIT). Vendored because its AUR package
# fails to build: the pinned sha256 of Codeberg's auto-generated tarball no longer
# matches. Enabled via kwinrc [Plugins] krohnkiteEnabled=true.
.local/share/kwin/scripts/krohnkite/

# YAMIS icons (opendesktop p/2303161, GPL 3). 20 MB: 3960 files + 2070 symlinks.
# Only vendorable because expand_entries matches -type l and the copy loop
# recreates links instead of dereferencing them.
.local/share/icons/YAMIS/

# NOTE: Scratchy.colors above is listed by name, not as the whole color-schemes/
# directory, because kde-material-you-colors also dumps generated MaterialYou*.colors
# there and a directory entry would pull those into the repo on every `save`.

# ── KWin: compositor, virtual desktops, tiling, window rules, Night Color ────
.config/kwinrc
.config/kwinrulesrc

# ── Plasma shell ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two files are deliberately NOT managed here, both owned by plasmashell:
#
#   plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc  the panel layout. plasmashell
#     rewrites it live and generates the containment/applet IDs inside it. The
#     panel is built by hand — see dots/kde/backup/README.md.
#
#   plasmashellrc  panel geometry keyed by those same generated IDs
#     ([PlasmaViews][Panel 222]), plus [Updates] performed= — the list of Plasma
#     migration scripts already run on THIS machine. Copying that to another
#     machine would make Plasma skip migrations it never actually performed.
.config/plasmarc

# ── Applications and session services ───────────────────────────────────────
.config/kdeglobals                  # theme, fonts, colors (also written by kde-material-you-colors)
.config/klipperrc                   # clipboard history
.config/spectaclerc                 # screenshots, recording, OCR languages
.config/krunnerrc                   # launcher
.config/kscreenlockerrc             # lock screen
.config/powermanagementprofilesrc   # idle, DPMS, suspend  (replaces hypridle)
.config/kactivitymanagerdrc
.config/breezerc
.config/dolphinrc
.config/kcminputrc                  # cursor theme + size (NOT in kdeglobals)

# ── Portals (Plasma session only) ───────────────────────────────────────────
.config/xdg-desktop-portal/kde-portals.conf

# ── Deliberately NOT managed ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .config/kwinoutputconfig.json  — per-machine monitor state, owned by KScreen
# .config/kscreen/               — idem
# .config/plasma-localerc        — set once by the initial setup wizard
